      "id": 1,
      "text": "Big Sandy began as a railroad town in 1887, quickly becoming a major shipping hub for sheep and cattle.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://discoverbigsandy.com/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "From 1997 to 2009, the world’s largest farm tractor, Big Bud 747, roamed Big Sandy before returning in 2020.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Sandy%2C_Montana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Big Sandy Historical Museum, housed by the local Historical Society, showcases artifacts and stories from the town’s pioneering past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Sandy%2C_Montana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Big Sandy is named after the nearby Big Sandy Creek, which once served as a vital water source for early settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Sandy%2C_Montana",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A historic water tower in Big Sandy once stood tall enough to be seen from many miles away.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Sandy%2C_Montana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Virgelle Ferry, a historic cable ferry, still operates across the Missouri River near Big Sandy.",
